lesson.m02.l11.title|Decision Gate
lesson.m02.l11.requirement|Use if to dispatch a harvest route only when a crop is detected.
feedback.m02.l11.construct|Add an if statement that guards the crop decision.
lesson.m02.l12.title|Fallback Route
lesson.m02.l12.requirement|Use else to select a safe route when the crop condition is false.
feedback.m02.l12.construct|Add an else branch for the fallback route.
lesson.m02.l13.title|Safe Harvest Condition
lesson.m02.l13.requirement|Combine crop and capacity checks with Boolean AND.
feedback.m02.l13.construct|Combine both conditions with &&.
lesson.m02.l14.title|Boolean Status
lesson.m02.l14.requirement|Store and use a Boolean readiness status before moving the robot.
lesson.m02.l15.title|Route Selector
lesson.m02.l15.requirement|Use switch to select an approved route mode.
feedback.m02.l15.construct|Use switch to select the route mode.
lesson.m02.l16.title|Station Cases
lesson.m02.l16.requirement|Handle each station mode with a case label.
feedback.m02.l16.construct|Add a case label for the selected station mode.
lesson.m02.l17.title|Safety Inversion
lesson.m02.l17.requirement|Use Boolean negation to stop an unsafe route.
feedback.m02.l17.construct|Use ! to express the unsafe condition.
lesson.m02.l18.title|Nested Inspection
lesson.m02.l18.requirement|Use a nested condition to inspect crop and depot state.
feedback.m02.l18.construct|Add an if condition for the inspection step.
lesson.m02.l19.title|Fault Response
lesson.m02.l19.requirement|Use switch to report a route fault and choose recovery.
feedback.m02.l19.construct|Use switch for the fault response.
lesson.m02.l20.title|Control Logic Assessment
lesson.m02.l20.requirement|Combine conditions and switch-based routing in a verified automation cycle.
feedback.m02.l20.construct|Use switch as part of the final control logic.
lesson.m03.l21.title|Repeated Row Route
lesson.m03.l21.requirement|Use for to harvest the five-crop multi-row route without repeating movement statements.
feedback.m03.l21.construct|Use a for loop to repeat the row route.
lesson.m03.l22.title|Inventory-Controlled Route
lesson.m03.l22.requirement|Use while to keep processing the route until the required harvest is collected.
feedback.m03.l22.construct|Use while for the inventory-controlled route.
lesson.m03.l23.title|First Inspection
lesson.m03.l23.requirement|Use do-while for an inspection that must execute before the route condition is checked.
feedback.m03.l23.construct|Use a do-while loop for the first inspection.
lesson.m03.l24.title|Field Sweep
lesson.m03.l24.requirement|Use nested for loops to sweep the two-dimensional field and harvest five crops.
feedback.m03.l24.construct|Use two for loops for the row-and-column sweep.
lesson.m03.l25.title|Iteration Counter
lesson.m03.l25.requirement|Use for to repeat a route while recording each harvest iteration.
feedback.m03.l25.construct|Use a for loop for the repeated iteration.
lesson.m03.l26.title|Blocked Point Skip
lesson.m03.l26.requirement|Use continue to skip a blocked inspection point and proceed with the route.
feedback.m03.l26.construct|Use continue when the inspection point is blocked.
lesson.m03.l27.title|Extended Route
lesson.m03.l27.requirement|Use while to process and deliver all six crops from the extended route.
feedback.m03.l27.construct|Use while to control the extended route.
lesson.m03.l28.title|Conditional Field Sweep
lesson.m03.l28.requirement|Use nested for loops and a condition to sweep the six-crop field safely.
feedback.m03.l28.construct|Use two for loops for the conditional field sweep.
lesson.m03.l29.title|Safety Stop
lesson.m03.l29.requirement|Use break to leave a route loop when a safety condition is reached.
feedback.m03.l29.construct|Use break to stop the route safely.
lesson.m03.l30.title|Iteration Assessment
lesson.m03.l30.requirement|Use nested loops to complete the six-crop automation route and deliver it to the depot.
feedback.m03.l30.construct|Use two for loops in the final iteration assessment.
lesson.m04.l31.title|Crop Navigation Helper
lesson.m04.l31.requirement|Declare move_to_crop to isolate movement toward a crop.
feedback.m04.l31.construct|Declare a callable move_to_crop function.
